tes successfully\n\nThe degraded performance is a **direct consequence of the configured label noise**, not an incident in the training infrastructure or code.\n\n### Conclusion\nThis run is **healthy**. The lower validation accuracy is the expected outcome of deliberately corrupting 42% of training labels. No fault has occurred; the system is functioning as designed with a challenging data configuration.",
